LUNE BROWSER




# ABOUT LUNE

A browser built from spare parts. Used by [@leebyron](https://leebyron.com) you can use it too.

Based on and inspired by:

 - [ungoogled-chromium](https://github.com/ungoogled-software/ungoogled-chromium/)
 - [helium](https://helium.computer/)
 - [xelium](https://github.com/minervanet/xelium-macos)
 - [arc browser](https://arc.net/)

## AGENT DOCUMENTATION

Documentation written by and for agents lives in `agent-docs/`.
Start with [the project definition](agent-docs/project/README.md).

 - [Repository and patch architecture](agent-docs/project/architecture.md)
 - [Builds, releases, and automatic updates](agent-docs/project/releases.md)
 - [Self-hosted services and website](agent-docs/project/services.md)
 - [Implementation roadmap](agent-docs/project/roadmap.md)
 - [Upstream research and sources](agent-docs/project/research.md)

Agent instructions are in [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md).

Current status: architecture, documentation, and minimal website bootstrap.
The initial target is macOS on Apple silicon and Intel; browser build and release
automation is not yet set up.

## WEBSITE

The static website lives in `website/public/` and deploys to Cloudflare Workers.
See [the deployment runbook](agent-docs/project/website.md) for setup and status.

